# Captured from vanilla 26.2 (protocol 776) survival oracle.
# Packet: clientbound set_entity_data for a `/summon item` drop of
# {id:"minecraft:diamond_pickaxe",count:1,
# components:{"minecraft:repair_cost":7}}.
#
# ..        VarInt entity id (session-scoped; not compared)
# 08        metadata index 8 = ItemEntity.DATA_ITEM
# 07        serializer 7 = ITEM_STACK
# 01        VarInt stack count = 1
# c6 07     VarInt item registry id 966 = minecraft:diamond_pickaxe
# 01        DataComponentPatch: 1 added
# 00        DataComponentPatch: 0 removed
# 13        component type id 19 = minecraft:repair_cost  <-- UNMODELED
# 07        its payload, which we cannot skip and never read
# ff        end-of-list sentinel, likewise never reached
#
# The last two bytes are deliberately NOT consumed: a clientbound
# patch length-prefixes neither itself nor its components, so an
# unmodeled one ends the decode in place. Reading on would take `07`
# as a metadata index and `ff` as a truncated serializer VarInt — a
# plausible-looking misparse, which is why the rest is abandoned.
a1 e4 01 08 07 01 c6 07 01 00 13 07 ff
